# the same string published at https://launchpad.net/~bceverly/+editpgpkeys
# and served by keyserver.ubuntu.com to anyone who asks. Nothing here is
# secret, and nothing here can sign anything.
#
# The private half lives in a password vault and in the
# LAUNCHPAD_GPG_PRIVATE_KEY GitHub secret, and nowhere else. It is never
# written into this repository in any form.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Which key signs restate's source packages for the Launchpad PPA -- the one
# tmd's are signed with, registered on the same Launchpad account.
#
# Pinned here, rather than taken from DEBSIGN_KEYID in the environment: that
# variable is global to a shell, and on a machine that maintains several
# packages it names whichever project was set up first. Which key signs this
# project is a property of this project.
#
# To use another key for one build without editing this file:
#     RESTATE_SIGNING_KEY=<fingerprint> make deb-source
#
# Format: one full 40-character fingerprint. Comments and blank lines ignored.

